[center][size=6][b]SkyParkour Together[/b][/size]
[size=4]Parkour Animations Sync for Skyrim Together Reborn[/size][/center]

Your friends see your parkour. When you vault a fence, climb a wall, grab a ledge, step up, slide or land in a roll with [b]SkyParkour[/b], everyone in your [b]Skyrim Together Reborn[/b] session sees the same animation on your character, at the same height and variant you got. No more watching a friend float up a cliff in a running pose.

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Every SkyParkour move is shared[/b]: vaults, climbs, low and high ledge grabs, steps (including weapon-out steps that play on the legs only), slides and landing rolls, at your playback speed setting.
[*][b]The same animation on every screen[/b]: the graph values SkyParkour uses to pick an animation go along with each move, so other players see the exact animation you played.
[*][b]One installer for three game versions[/b]: Skyrim [b]1.5.97[/b], [b]1.6.1170 / 1.6.1179[/b] and [b]1.7.104[/b]. The FOMOD asks which one you play.
[*][b]No server changes[/b]: it plays on any regular Skyrim Together Reborn 1.8.5 server.
[*][b]SkyParkour itself is untouched[/b]: this mod contains no SkyParkour files and changes nothing about how parkour plays for you.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[b]Every player in the session[/b] needs all of these:
[list]
[*]Skyrim Special/Anniversary Edition [b]1.5.97, 1.6.1170, 1.6.1179 or 1.7.104[/b]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url] for your game version
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/69993]Skyrim Together Reborn[/url] [b]1.8.5[/b] for your game version
[*][b]SkyParkour[/b] by Tsptds, from its own Nexus page (not included)
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install Skyrim Together Reborn 1.8.5 and SkyParkour as usual.
[*]Install this mod with Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex and pick your game version in the installer.
[*]Let it win its file conflict with Skyrim Together Reborn: in MO2, place it [b]below[/b] Skyrim Together Reborn in the left pane; in Vortex, set it to load [b]after[/b].
[*]Start the game from [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherRuntime/SkyrimTogether.exe[/font], as you normally start Skyrim Together.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Is it working?[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/SkyParkourTogether.log[/font] says [i]"Skyrim Together add-on found"[/i].
[*]Skyrim Together's log ([font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherRuntime/logs[/font]) contains [i]"mod sync: SkyParkour Together 1.0.0 ... registered"[/i].
[/list]
If the SKSE log says the add-on was [b]not[/b] found, another mod's [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] is winning: fix the conflict order (step 3).

[size=5][b]How it works[/b][/size]
SkyParkour plays its animations directly on your character's animation graph, which Skyrim Together does not share, so other players only saw you slide around in a running pose. This mod has two parts:
[list]
[*][b]SkyParkourTogether.dll[/b] (SKSE plugin): tells Skyrim Together which of your animations are SkyParkour's and which values pick the right one. It reads no game memory, so one DLL works on every game version.
[*][b]SkyrimTogether.exe[/b] for your game version: Skyrim Together Reborn 1.8.5 with a small add-on, the [i]STR Mod Sync API[/i], that sends those animations through Skyrim Together's existing animation relay and plays them on your character on the other players' screens. Nothing else in Skyrim Together is changed. On 1.5.97 the installer also adds the files Skyrim Together needs to run on that version.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Other mods that replace SkyrimTogether.exe[/b] (other Skyrim Together forks or patches) conflict with this mod: only one launcher can win.
[*]Works alongside other SkyParkour add-ons and animation mods.
[*]Mods that add their own parkour animation events outside SkyParkour's names are not shared.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Remove the mod. Skyrim Together's own [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] takes over again.

[size=5][b]Credits[/b][/size]
